('battle-battle-of-mannar-1658', 'The Battle of Mannar was a short battle fought between the Dutch and the opposing Portuguese forces on 22 February 1658. This battle, along with the subsequent capture of Jaffna would mark the end of Portuguese Ceylon. The site lay outside every kingdom mapped in the atlas that year.', 'The Battle of Mannar was a short battle fought between the Dutch and the opposing Portuguese forces on 22 February 1658. This battle, along with the subsequent capture of Jaffna would mark the end of Portuguese Ceylon. The battle location is not recorded here.', 79.8333, 9.05, true, ARRAY[]::text[]),
('battle-battle-of-pratapgarh-1659', 'The Battle of Pratapgad took place on 10 November 1659, at Pratapgad in Satara. The battle was fought between the Maratha forces led by Shivaji Maharaj and the Bijapur troops under General Afzal Khan. The Maratha emerged victorious, marking their first significant military triumph against a major regional power. The site lay within the borders of Bijapur Sultanate that year (per Cliopatria).', 'The Battle of Pratapgad took place on 10 November 1659, at Pratapgad in Satara. The battle was fought between the Maratha forces led by Shivaji Maharaj and the Bijapur troops under General Afzal Khan. The Maratha emerged victorious, marking their first significant military triumph against a major regional power. The battle location is not recorded here.', 73.5776, 17.9362, true, ARRAY['bijapur']::text[]),
('battle-battle-of-khajwa-1659', 'The Battle of Khajuha was fought on January 5, 1659, between the newly crowned Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb and Shah Shuja who also declared himself Mughal Emperor in Bengal. Shuja''s army rested by the tank of Khajwa, about 30 miles to the west of Fatehpur-
